# Anchored, for the same reason `logs/` below is: unanchored, `data/` matches a
# directory of that name at *any* depth, and it silently swallowed
# `qa/regression-suite/data/` — a whole cluster of the QA regression suite,
# which git would never have offered to add and no `git status` would mention.
# The root `data/` this is actually for is a running instance's scratch.
/data/
# Anchored to the repository root: this is for runtime log output a running
# instance drops beside the code. Unanchored, it also swallowed
# `docs/qa/logs/`, which is the QA evidence — checked-in documentation that
# happens to live in a directory called logs. A test log nobody can review
# because version control quietly discarded it is worth nothing.
/logs/

# JetBrains project files — local to one developer's machine.
.idea/
